---
import { t, type Locale } from "../lib/i18n";

/**
 * About page body.
 *
 * Both editions live here, but only one is ever rendered — Astro evaluates the
 * branch at build time, so the built page contains a single language.
 */
interface Props {
  lang: Locale;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;

const DEBP =
  "https://www.edb.gov.hk/en/edu-system/primary-secondary/applicable-to-primary-secondary/it-in-edu/debp.html";
---

{
  lang === "zh-HK" ? (
    <>
      <h1>{t(lang, "navAbout")}</h1>

      <p>
        BEETS AI 是一個<strong>免費的香港 AI 教學資源庫</strong>，按學科、級別和具體教學需要，
        提供可編輯的工作紙、教案及校本規劃範例。
      </p>

      <h2>編輯流程</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>選題：以教師的具體需要為單位（級別 + 學科 + 任務），而不是泛泛的主題。</li>
        <li>草擬：內容由 AI 協助草擬與排版。</li>
        <li>核實：每一項事實與數字，均對照列明的官方來源逐項核對。</li>
        <li>審閱：由教育工作者審核學習目標、準確度、年齡適切性和課堂可行性。</li>
        <li>發佈：通過上述關卡後才會上線。</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="meta">每次建置都會自動檢查連結；每份資源在發佈前都對照其列明的來源逐項核實。</p>

      <h2>獨立性</h2>
      <p>
        本網站為 Beets 獨立製作的資源計劃，<strong>並非 EDB 官方文件</strong>。
        我們引用並連結官方文件，但教材內容與判斷由我們自行負責。如發現錯誤，歡迎聯絡我們更正。
      </p>

      <h2>來源文件</h2>
      <p>資源頁所列的來源代碼，對應以下教育局文件：</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>B</strong> — 數字教育藍圖單張（DEBP 三摺頁）</li>
        <li><strong>F</strong> — 《人工智能素養學習框架》（中小學）</li>
        <li><strong>G</strong> — 《在教學中使用人工智能的指引》（中小學）</li>
        <li><strong>E</strong> — 人工智能教育應用示例</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        官方文件與相關資源：<a href={DEBP} rel="noopener">{t(lang, "debpLinkText")}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>回饋與請求</h2>
      <p>
        你用過我們的資源嗎？哪一份需要改善？想我們製作哪一份？歡迎在任一資源頁留言告訴我們，
        或直接聯絡 Beets 團隊。你的回饋會直接影響下一批資源的選題。
      </p>

      <h2>使用條款與私隱</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>資源可免費下載，供教學使用及改編；請保留來源標示。</li>
        <li>若引用第三方教材，我們會連結原始來源；重製前會先確認授權。</li>
        <li>本站不收集學生作品或任何可識別學生身分的資料。</li>
        <li>下載不需註冊；如有提供電郵，只會在取得同意後用作通知新資源。</li>
      </ul>
    </>
  ) : (
    <>
      <h1>{t(lang, "navAbout")}</h1>

      <p>
        BEETS AI is a <strong>free library of Hong Kong AI teaching resources</strong>, organised by
        subject, learning stage and specific classroom task — editable worksheets, lesson plans and
        school-planning examples.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial process</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose the topic: one teacher need (stage + subject + task), never a vague theme.</li>
        <li>Draft: the content is drafted and typeset with AI assistance.</li>
        <li>Verify: every fact and figure is checked against the official source cited on the page.</li>
        <li>
          Review: an educator checks the learning aim, accuracy, age-appropriateness and classroom
          fit.
        </li>
        <li>Publish: nothing goes live until it has passed those gates.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="meta">
        Links are checked automatically on every build, and every resource is fact-checked against
        its cited sources before publication.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        This site is an independent resource initiative by Beets. It is{" "}
        <strong>not an official EDB publication</strong>. We quote and link the official documents,
        but the teaching material and the judgements in it are ours. If you find an error, tell us
        and we will correct it.
      </p>

      <h2>Source documents</h2>
      <p>
        The source codes on our resource pages refer to these Education Bureau documents (titles
        translated for this English edition — follow the link below for the official publications):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>B</strong> — Digital Education Blueprint leaflet (the DEBP three-fold leaflet)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>F</strong> — the EDB AI literacy learning framework (primary and secondary)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>G</strong> — the EDB guidelines on using AI in teaching (primary and secondary)
        </li>
        <li><strong>E</strong> — the EDB examples of AI applications in education</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Official documents and related material:{" "}
        <a href={DEBP} rel="noopener">{t(lang, "debpLinkText")}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Feedback and requests</h2>
      <p>
        Have you used our resources? Which one needs improving? Which one should we make next? Tell
        us on any resource page, or contact the Beets team directly. Your feedback decides what we
        build next.
      </p>

      <h2>Reuse and privacy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Download and adapt the resources freely for teaching; please keep the attribution.</li>
        <li>
          Where third-party material is used, we link the original source and confirm reuse terms
          before republishing.
        </li>
        <li>We collect no student work and nothing that could identify a student.</li>
        <li>
          Downloads need no registration; an email address is only used, with consent, to tell you
          about new resources.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </>
  )
}
